The plan reviewer found three blocking sequencing/interface issues, all valid:

- coverage invalidation was scheduled before the completeness field existed;
- the extractor returned only a union, so lifecycle code couldn’t finalize a specific child turn;
- SessionEnd could miss a follow-up turn when an older completed task record still occupied that child’s slot.

I’m revising both the implementation plan and the ignored design spec: establish completeness primitives earlier, expose per-child analysis results, and sweep every observed-but-unfinalized ledger turn at SessionEnd—not merely currently “live” task records.

